name c01m06-four-of-a-kind
timeout 900
time 1996-03-23T06:00:00Z

# F-22 LIGHTNING II (NovaLogic 1996), CAMPAIGN ONE, SORTIE 1.6 OF 8 — "FOUR OF A KIND".
# Spec: mods/f22/doc/campaign.md 2. Geometry: mods/f22/doc/terrain.md 3. Substitutions:
# mods/f22/doc/substitutions.md. The five campaign-wide disclosures: c01m01-snake-eyes.fbm.
#
# THE TASK [TXT]: escort four C-5 Galaxy of Mule Squadron, briefed 65 NM W; measured 65.3 NM on
# bearing 246.2 deg [ORF] — the campaign's WORST briefing bearing, 23.8 deg off the stated octant, and
# the single number that shows the prose cannot place anything (campaign.md 5).
#
# SUBSTITUTIONS IN THIS FILE
#   C-5A/B Galaxy -> `kc135` x 4. Same reasoning as the An-225 of sortie 1.4: the catalogue's only
#     large four-engine jet. Span 39.88 m against the C-5's 67.9 m, cruise 237 m/s against ~245 m/s.
#     The speed is right; the span is 59 % of the original, so — again — visual acquisition of the
#     thing being escorted happens LATER here than it would against the real aircraft.
#   AWACS (`AWACS.PAK` [ORF]) -> `e3` (E-3 Sentry). The manual's friendly list names an E-767; the
#     catalogue has the E-3, which is the same airframe family and the same role. It holds an orbit and
#     publishes an `FBNetReport` — an anonymous point with its own look age, no identity, no team. It
#     is NOT wired into a `net` block here: the escorts are `NetMember` rows, but nothing in any source
#     read says the game's AWACS cued anybody, and wiring one would be inventing doctrine.
#   MiG-27 / MiG-29 "from the north" [TXT] -> `mig23` + `mig29`, one each.
#
# WHY THE VERDICT SITS ON `s6esc1` AND THE KILLS ON `s6esc2`. campaign.md's reading rule: "own kills
# are irrelevant to the verdict and must not enter it." But an uncovered death ends the run CRASH/exit
# 2, so somebody has to declare the two interceptors. Split, exactly as in 1.4: `s6esc1` carries FOUR
# `protect` lines and nothing else, `s6esc2` carries the two `kill`s. The sortie's verdict is
# `s6esc1`'s UNIT_RESULT, and no kill can reach it.
#
# THE FOUR GALAXIES CARRY A ROUTE AND NO `objective` LINE, WHICH IS DELIBERATE. Without objectives the
# flight plan IS the verdict (doc/missions/verdict.md), so each Mule's own UNIT_RESULT answers exactly
# campaign.md's condition — "all four alive at their exit waypoint" — without a second mechanism. A
# Galaxy that dies is a mission catastrophe and shows up as its own FAIL plus `s6esc1`'s violated
# `protect`, in the same run, from two independent judges.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `s6esc1`'s UNIT_RESULT.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 = all four `protect` met and Escort Lead combat-effective at the end; the four
#   `mule` UNIT_RESULTs must independently read SUCCESS, and if the two disagree that IS the finding.
#   `s6esc1` FAIL with a violated `protect` = a Galaxy was lost. Name which one; that is the whole
#   report of this sortie.
#   `s6esc2`'s two kills are NOT the verdict under any outcome. An escort that shoots nobody down and
#   brings four Galaxies home has flown this sortie perfectly.
#   exit 3 with everything met except a Mule's waypoints = the transports were slow, not shot. Read
#   `activeWp` in their telemetry before reporting anything.

# MEASURED (exit 3): ALL FOUR GALAXIES HOME, NOBODY SHOT DOWN, AND THE SORTIE IS A SUCCESS.
#   t = 378.3 / 378.4 / 704.0 / 704.6 s   `s6mul1..4` each `all waypoints reached`
#   t = 900.0 s         `s6esc1` SUCCESS — four `protect` met, `survive` met
#                       `s6esc2` TIMEOUT — both `kill` unmet; the two interceptors were never brought
#                       to a firing solution and both survive
#   THE EXIT CODE IS 3 AND THE SORTIE PASSED. This is the file the campaign's split-declaration device
#   exists for: an escort that shoots nobody down and delivers four transports has done its job, and
#   the only unit whose verdict says so is `s6esc1`.
#   The two Mule pairs finish 326 s apart — 1/2 at t = 378, 3/4 at t = 704 — because they are declared
#   2 km abeam each other on the same two waypoints and the outer pair's capture geometry differs. Not
#   a defect; noted so nobody reads it as one.

unit s6esc1
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm6 1
  spawn 18.58090 99.75041 6000 246.2 480      # 52 km down-corridor, ahead of and above the transports
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 18.39240 99.29976 6000 480               # the Mule waypoint [ORF] 65.3 NM / 246.2 deg from Tyler
  objective protect unit s6mul1
  objective protect unit s6mul2
  objective protect unit s6mul3
  objective protect unit s6mul4
  objective survive

unit s6esc2
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight storm6 2
  spawn 18.59323 99.74467 6000 246.2 480      # 1.5 km across corridor from the escort lead
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set store 8 aim120
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 480
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 19.47037 99.29976 6000 480               # north, toward where the interceptors come from
  objective kill unit s6mig1
  objective kill unit s6mig2
  objective survive

unit s6mul1
  module kc135
  team friendly
  spawn 18.60990 99.81979 7000 246.2 460      # 60 km short of the Mule waypoint
  wp 18.39240 99.29976 7000 460
  wp 18.28364 99.03999 7000 460               # the exit waypoint, 30 km beyond

unit s6mul2
  module kc135
  team friendly
  spawn 18.62634 99.81213 7000 246.2 460      # 2 km abeam
  wp 18.39240 99.29976 7000 460
  wp 18.28364 99.03999 7000 460

unit s6mul3
  module kc135
  team friendly
  spawn 18.64278 99.80448 7000 246.2 460      # 4 km abeam
  wp 18.39240 99.29976 7000 460
  wp 18.28364 99.03999 7000 460

unit s6mul4
  module kc135
  team friendly
  spawn 18.65922 99.79683 7000 246.2 460      # 6 km abeam
  wp 18.39240 99.29976 7000 460
  wp 18.28364 99.03999 7000 460

unit s6awx
  module e3
  team friendly
  spawn 18.66428 99.94990 9000 246.2 240      # behind the package, on station
  set orbit 60000 900
  set drag_threat_s 0                         # ordered to hold the orbit: the honest way to say "never runs"
  wp 18.55553 99.68972 9000 240

unit s6mig1
  module mig23
  team hostile
  spawn 19.47037 99.29976 6000 180.0 450      # 120 km due north of the corridor
  set gear up
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 180 120 6000
  set store 1 r24r
  set store 2 r24r
  set brief_master_arm arm
  wp 18.39240 99.29976 6000 450
  objective survive

unit s6mig2
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 19.47037 99.27117 6000 180.0 450      # 3 km abeam its leader
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 7 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 18.39240 99.29976 6000 450
  objective survive
